1
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:02,052
Hi again.

2
00:00:02,052 --> 00:00:04,690
This module featured a lot of information.

3
00:00:04,690 --> 00:00:08,708
We revisited familiar concepts and
introduced so many new ones.

4
00:00:08,708 --> 00:00:12,739
We discussed quality management, where
we learned the four steps to ensuring

5
00:00:12,739 --> 00:00:16,650
quality, which includes setting
quality standards, quality planning,

6
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:19,108
quality assurance, and quality control.

7
00:00:19,108 --> 00:00:24,316
We covered continuous improvement and
how to use data driven strategies such

8
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:29,618
as DMAIC, which stands for Define,
Measure, Analyze, Improve, Control.

9
00:00:29,618 --> 00:00:33,548
And PDCA, which stands for
Plan, Do, Check,

10
00:00:33,548 --> 00:00:38,226
act in order to work toward
continuous improvements.

11
00:00:38,226 --> 00:00:41,477
We learned how to conduct and
use retrospectives as a tool for

12
00:00:41,477 --> 00:00:42,763
future improvements.

13
00:00:42,763 --> 00:00:47,008
And how to facilitate positive
conversation and encourage feedback

14
00:00:47,008 --> 00:00:52,010
from your team members in order to avoid
mistakes later on in future projects.

15
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:55,492
I'm really proud of how far you've come,
and I hope you are too.

16
00:00:55,492 --> 00:00:59,490
I hope you take a moment to admire
your progress and applaud yourself.

17
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:03,234
In the next module, you'll learn about
the importance of gathering data and

18
00:01:03,234 --> 00:01:05,050
how to make data driven decisions.

19
00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:07,850
I'll meet you there whenever you're ready.
